s1-p26 : Block
s1-p26 = prose (cons "Correctness is relative to the selected \(P\), not a verdict attached to \(f\) in isolation. Constructing behavior that satisfies a requirement already includes the reasoning that establishes the requirement. Expressing that reasoning in the language of the construction preserves it for further use rather than discarding it or translating it into a separate verification model. Zero marginal proof-writing beyond the reasoning already required is the design objective. Tests observe selected executions, whereas \(q\) concerns every input in its stated domain. Correctness conditions and the reasoning required to establish them have a long programming-methodology lineage, including Dijkstra's treatment of program construction ([68](#ref-68))." nil)
